[ti:PyTorch 2.10: Faster Kernels, Safer Numbers, and a New Release Rhythm]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: If you're training large models, a tiny numerical difference can turn into a very long debugging session.
[00:00.00]Ava：训练大模型时，一点数值差异就可能让你调试很久。
[00:08.38]And a little kernel overhead can quietly slow down every step. PyTorch 2.
[00:08.38]而一点内核开销也会悄悄拖慢每一步。PyTorch 2.
[00:14.20]10 is aimed at both problems.
[00:14.20]10 正是为解决这两个问题而来。
[00:16.86]Brian: Exactly.
[00:16.86]Brian：没错。
[00:17.48]This release pushes performance, but it also makes numerical behavior easier to inspect.
[00:17.48]这个版本提升了性能，也让数值行为更容易检查。
[00:24.32]It adds Python 3. 14 support for torch.
[00:24.32]它新增了 Python 3.14 对 torch.
[00:27.35]compile(), new attention and fusion features, and tools for finding where two runs start to disagree.
[00:27.35]compile() 的支持，还带来新的注意力与融合功能，以及定位两次运行从哪里开始出现差异的工具。
[00:35.55]Ava: Let's start with the big picture. What changed in this release?
[00:35.55]Ava：先看整体。这次发布有哪些变化？
[00:40.17]Brian: PyTorch 2.
[00:40.17]Brian：再看 PyTorch 2.
[00:40.92]10 contains four thousand one hundred sixty commits from five hundred thirty-six contributors since 2.
[00:40.92]10 版收录了 536 位贡献者的 4160 次提交，从 2.
[00:48.59]9.
[00:48.59]9 版算起。
[00:48.74]The article groups the changes into performance, numerical debugging, and some non-feature updates.
[00:48.74]文章将这些变化分为性能、数值调试和其他非功能更新。
[00:56.53]Ava: And the release is part of the larger two-series compiler story, right?
[00:56.53]Ava：这次发布也是整个 2.x 系列编译器发展的一部分，对吧？
[01:02.16]Brian: Yes.
[01:02.16]Brian：是的。
[01:02.45]Performance has been a focus throughout the two-x releases, building on the PyTorch compiler stack introduced in 2.
[01:02.45]整个 2.x 系列都在持续提升性能，基础是 PyTorch 在 2.
[01:10.83]0. In 2.
[01:10.83]0 版引入的编译器体系。在 2.
[01:11.42]10, that means more work in torchinductor, more compiler support, and better ways to test numerical behavior.
[01:11.42]10 版中，torchinductor 得到更多改进，编译器支持更广，数值行为也更容易测试。
[01:19.72]Ava: Let's talk about the kernel work first. I saw the phrase Combo Kernels.
[01:19.72]Ava：先聊内核方面的改进。我看到了“Combo Kernels”这个词。
[01:24.78]What does that actually mean?
[01:24.78]它具体是什么意思？
[01:27.19]Brian: Combo Kernels are a horizontal fusion optimization in torchinductor.
[01:27.19]Brian：Combo Kernels 是 torchinductor 中的一项横向融合优化。
[01:32.66]They combine multiple independent operations, with no data dependencies, into one unified GPU kernel.
[01:32.66]它把多个没有数据依赖关系的独立操作合并成一个 GPU 内核。
[01:41.13]Ava: So this is different from the usual producer-consumer fusion?
[01:41.13]Ava：这和常见的生产者与消费者融合不同？
[01:45.20]Brian: Right.
[01:45.20]Brian：对。
[01:45.64]Vertical fusion combines sequential operations, where one operation produces data for the next.
[01:45.64]纵向融合会合并前后相继的操作，前一个操作为后一个提供数据。
[01:52.66]Combo Kernels fuse parallel operations instead.
[01:52.66]Combo Kernels 则融合并行操作。
[01:56.13]Imagine several small checkout lines merging into one larger line, even though none of the customers depend on one another.
[01:56.13]想象几条短的结账队伍汇成一条长队，尽管顾客之间互不依赖。
[02:05.56]Ava: The benefit is fewer kernel launches?
[02:05.56]Ava：好处是减少内核启动次数？
[02:08.65]Brian: That's the goal: reduced kernel launch overhead.
[02:08.65]Brian：对，目的是降低内核启动开销。
[02:12.09]The article doesn't give a benchmark number, but it explains that independent operations can now share one launch.
[02:12.09]文章没有给出基准测试数据，但解释了独立操作现在可以共用一次启动。
[02:20.25]The feature is marked API-UNSTABLE, so users should expect it to evolve.
[02:20.25]这项功能标记为 API-UNSTABLE，用户应预期它还会变化。
[02:25.75]Ava: The next item is varlen_attn(). The name sounds like variable-length attention.
[02:25.75]Ava：下一项是 varlen_attn()。听名字像是变长注意力。
[02:32.68]Brian: That's exactly what it is. varlen_attn() is a new torch. nn.
[02:32.68]Brian：正是。varlen_attn() 是 torch.nn 中的新型
[02:37.18]attention operation for ragged and packed sequences.
[02:37.18]注意力算子，适用于不规则序列和打包序列。
[02:41.09]Ragged means the sequences can have different lengths, and packed means they can be stored together without padding every item to the same size.
[02:41.09]不规则序列的长度可以不同；打包序列则能存放在一起，无须把每个序列填充到相同长度。
[02:52.25]Ava: Does it support training, or only inference?
[02:52.25]Ava：它支持训练，还是只支持推理？
[02:56.03]Brian: It supports both forward and backward, and it's torch. compile-able.
[02:56.03]Brian：前向和反向计算都支持，也可以用 torch.compile 编译。
[03:01.37]Right now, FlashAttention 2, or FA2, supports it.
[03:01.37]目前，FlashAttention 2（FA2）支持它。
[03:05.22]The article says there are plans to add cuDNN and FlashAttention 4 support.
[03:05.22]文章说，未来计划加入 cuDNN 和 FlashAttention 4 支持。
[03:11.46]Ava: What hardware and data types are supported?
[03:11.46]Ava：支持哪些硬件和数据类型？
[03:14.88]Brian: For now, it runs on NVIDIA CUDA with an A100 GPU or newer.
[03:14.88]Brian：目前支持 NVIDIA CUDA，GPU 需为 A100 或更新型号。
[03:20.07]It supports BF16 and FP16 data types.
[03:20.07]支持 BF16 和 FP16 数据类型。
[03:23.39]Again, this is API-UNSTABLE, so those boundaries may change later.
[03:23.39]同样，它标记为 API-UNSTABLE，这些支持范围以后可能变化。
[03:29.65]Ava: Variable-length attention can save work because you don't calculate attention on padding, right?
[03:29.65]Ava：变长注意力能省去填充位置上的计算，对吧？
[03:36.39]Brian: That is the practical intuition, although the article focuses on the API and its current support rather than giving a measured speedup.
[03:36.39]Brian：实际意义可以这么理解。不过文章重点介绍的是 API 和当前支持情况，没有给出实测加速数据。
[03:44.78]The important point is that ragged and packed sequences now have a dedicated operation that works with compilation and gradients.
[03:44.78]关键是，不规则序列和打包序列现在有了专用算子，而且支持编译和梯度计算。
[03:53.15]Ava: There is also an eigenvalue update. That sounds more specialized.
[03:53.15]Ava：特征值计算也有更新。听起来更专门一些。
[03:59.24]Brian: It is more specialized, but useful for numerical workloads.
[03:59.24]Brian：是更专门，但对数值计算很有用。
[04:03.78]PyTorch linalg can now use cuSOLVER's DnXgeev to provide highly efficient general eigenvalue decomposition on NVIDIA GPUs.
[04:03.78]PyTorch linalg 现在可以调用 cuSOLVER 的 DnXgeev，在 NVIDIA GPU 上高效完成一般特征值分解。
[04:13.53]Ava: So PyTorch is connecting its linear algebra path to a more efficient cuSOLVER routine?
[04:13.53]Ava：所以 PyTorch 的线性代数功能接入了效率更高的 cuSOLVER 例程？
[04:20.19]Brian: Yes.
[04:20.19]Brian：对。
[04:20.49]That's the whole claim in the release note: use DnXgeev through cuSOLVER for efficient general eigenvalue decompositions on NVIDIA GPUs.
[04:20.49]发布说明的主张就是：在 NVIDIA GPU 上通过 cuSOLVER 使用 DnXgeev，高效完成一般特征值分解。
[04:30.58]The article doesn't provide a performance figure.
[04:30.58]文章没有提供性能数据。
[04:34.56]Ava: What about Intel GPUs? The release notes list several changes there.
[04:34.56]Ava：Intel GPU 呢？发布说明列出了几项相关更新。
[04:40.43]Brian: The support expands to the latest Intel Core Ultra Series 3 with Intel Arc Graphics, on both Windows and Linux.
[04:40.43]Brian：支持范围扩展到搭载 Intel Arc Graphics 的最新 Intel Core Ultra Series 3，覆盖 Windows 和 Linux。
[04:49.92]PyTorch also adds FP8 support on Intel GPUs.
[04:49.92]PyTorch 还为 Intel GPU 增加了 FP8 支持。
[04:54.03]Ava: FP8 support can mean a lot of different things. What does this release include?
[04:54.03]Ava：FP8 支持可能涵盖很多内容。这次具体包含什么？
[04:59.87]Brian: It adds commonly used basic operators, such as type promotion and shape operators, plus scaled matrix multiplication using tensor-wise and channel-wise scaling factors.
[04:59.87]Brian：包括类型提升、形状算子等常用基础算子，以及使用按张量和按通道缩放因子的缩放矩阵乘法。
[05:11.22]Ava: Anything beyond FP8?
[05:11.22]Ava：除了 FP8，还有别的吗？
[05:13.77]Brian: Yes. Aten operator MatMul gets complex data type support on Intel GPUs.
[05:13.77]Brian：有。Intel GPU 上的 Aten MatMul 算子现在支持复数数据类型。
[05:20.09]The PyTorch C++ Extension API also extends SYCL support, so users can implement new custom operators on Windows.
[05:20.09]PyTorch C++ Extension API 也扩展了 SYCL 支持，让用户能在 Windows 上实现新的自定义算子。
[05:30.06]And Intel GPU unit-test coverage is broadened.
[05:30.06]Intel GPU 的单元测试覆盖范围也扩大了。
[05:34.50]Ava: Now let's move to determinism. Why is this becoming such a big issue?
[05:34.50]Ava：接下来谈确定性。为什么它变得这么重要？
[05:40.44]Brian: The article connects it to post-training with distributed reinforcement learning workflows.
[05:40.44]Brian：文章将它与分布式强化学习流程中的后训练联系起来。
[05:46.81]At that scale, run-to-run determinism makes debugging training runs easier.
[05:46.81]在这种规模下，多次运行结果保持确定性，能让训练调试更容易。
[05:52.07]It also helps people test code that uses torch. compile reliably.
[05:52.07]这也有助于可靠地测试使用 torch.compile 的代码。
[05:56.97]Ava: What changed in 2. 10?
[05:56.97]Ava：2.10 有什么变化？
[06:00.29]Brian: torch. compile() now respects use_deterministic_mode.
[06:00.29]Brian：torch.compile() 现在会遵循 use_deterministic_mode。
[06:04.99]Users can turn deterministic algorithms on with torch.
[06:04.99]用户可以通过以下调用开启确定性算法：
[06:09.77]use_deterministic_algorithms(True).
[06:09.77]调用 torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True) 即可。
[06:12.87]The article says this makes two invocations of torch.
[06:12.87]文章说，两次调用 torch.compile
[06:17.56]compile perform the same operations exactly.
[06:17.56]会执行完全相同的操作。
[06:21.81]Ava: That sounds stronger than just getting similar outputs.
[06:21.81]Ava：这听起来比输出结果相近更进一步。
[06:25.95]Brian: Yes, the wording is about performing the same operations exactly.
[06:25.95]Brian：对，原文强调的是执行完全相同的操作。
[06:30.68]For someone chasing a rare divergence, that gives a much steadier baseline.
[06:30.68]追查偶发的结果偏差时，这能提供更稳定的基准。
[06:36.48]Ava: And then there's DebugMode. Is it a profiler?
[06:36.48]Ava：还有 DebugMode。它是性能分析器吗？
[06:40.48]Brian: It's a custom TorchDispatchMode that provides profiling-style runtime dumps.
[06:40.48]Brian：它是一种自定义 TorchDispatchMode，可生成类似性能分析记录的运行时转储。
[06:45.93]Its purpose here is numerical debugging: tracking dispatched calls and isolating numerical divergence.
[06:45.93]它在这里用于数值调试：追踪派发调用，定位数值偏差。
[06:53.60]Ava: How does it find the first bad operation?
[06:53.60]Ava：它怎么找到第一个出问题的操作？
[06:56.61]Brian: The key feature is tensor hashing.
[06:56.61]Brian：关键功能是张量哈希。
[06:58.91]You run two versions of a model with the same input, and you expect corresponding tensors to have the same deterministic hash.
[06:58.91]用相同输入运行模型的两个版本，预期对应张量会得到相同的确定性哈希值。
[07:07.44]You then look for the point where the hashes stop matching.
[07:07.44]然后找出哈希值从哪里开始不一致。
[07:11.44]That operation is often where the behavior starts to differ.
[07:11.44]行为往往就是从那个操作开始出现差异的。
[07:15.85]Ava: So instead of comparing only the final loss, you compare the whole trail of tensors.
[07:15.85]Ava：所以不只比较最终的损失值，还要比较沿途的所有张量。
[07:22.32]Brian: Exactly.
[07:22.32]Brian：正是这样。
[07:22.87]It's like checking every station on a train route instead of discovering at the final station that something went wrong.
[07:22.87]就像沿途逐站检查，而不是到了终点才发现出了问题。
[07:31.08]DebugMode also records dispatched operations and TorchInductor-compiled Triton kernels.
[07:31.08]DebugMode 还会记录派发的操作和由 TorchInductor 编译的 Triton 内核。
[07:37.38]Ava: Can engineers add their own information to those records?
[07:37.38]Ava：工程师能在这些记录中加入自己的信息吗？
[07:41.52]Brian: Yes. Dispatch hooks let users register custom hooks to annotate calls.
[07:41.52]Brian：能。派发钩子允许用户注册自定义钩子，为调用添加注释。
[07:47.01]The article presents three main capabilities: runtime logging, tensor hashing, and dispatch hooks.
[07:47.01]文章介绍了三项主要能力：运行时日志、张量哈希和派发钩子。
[07:55.05]Ava: Are these production-ready APIs?
[07:55.05]Ava：这些 API 可以用于生产环境了吗？
[07:57.97]Brian: The numerical debugging features are also labeled API-UNSTABLE.
[07:57.97]Brian：这些数值调试功能也被标记为 API-UNSTABLE。
[08:02.23]The article points readers to a tutorial for details, so teams should read that before building a long-term workflow around them.
[08:02.23]文章提供了教程链接，团队若要长期使用这些功能，应先读教程。
[08:11.32]Ava: Let's cover the non-feature updates. TorchScript is now deprecated.
[08:11.32]Ava：再谈谈功能之外的更新。TorchScript 现在已弃用。
[08:17.07]Brian: Correct. In PyTorch 2. 10, TorchScript is deprecated, and the article says torch.
[08:17.07]Brian：对。在 PyTorch 2.10 中，TorchScript 已弃用，文章建议
[08:23.25]export should be used instead.
[08:23.25]改用 torch.export。
[08:25.54]It points to a talk from the PyTorch Technical Committee for more detail.
[08:25.54]文章还推荐了一场 PyTorch 技术委员会的演讲，供读者了解详情。
[08:31.46]Ava: That could affect older deployment pipelines.
[08:31.46]Ava：这可能影响较早的部署流程。
[08:35.01]Brian: It could, especially if they still depend on TorchScript.
[08:35.01]Brian：确实，尤其是仍依赖 TorchScript 的流程。
[08:38.95]The release blog doesn't provide a migration timeline, so the safe takeaway is to start evaluating torch.
[08:38.95]发布博客没有给出迁移时间表，所以稳妥的做法是开始评估
[08:46.23]export and consult the linked guidance.
[08:46.23]torch.export，并参考文中链接的指南。
[08:49.28]Ava: There is also tlparse and TORCH_TRACE for compiler bug reports.
[08:49.28]Ava：编译器问题报告还可以用 tlparse 和 TORCH_TRACE。
[08:54.50]What problem do they solve?
[08:54.50]它们解决什么问题？
[08:57.09]Brian: Sometimes a compiler issue is too complex for a small standalone reproduction.
[08:57.09]Brian：有些编译器问题太复杂，难以写成简短的独立复现案例。
[09:02.68]tlparse results provide a log format that's easier to upload and share on GitHub.
[09:02.68]tlparse 的输出是更方便上传到 GitHub 分享的日志。
[09:08.48]Even people outside the PyTorch project can extract useful information from those logs.
[09:08.48]即使不是 PyTorch 项目成员，也能从这些日志中提取有用信息。
[09:15.06]Ava: So attaching a tlparse artifact can give maintainers more context than a short description?
[09:15.06]Ava：所以附上 tlparse 产物，比简短描述更能帮助维护者了解问题？
[09:21.77]Brian: That's the idea.
[09:21.77]Brian：正是如此。
[09:22.96]The article encourages users to attach tlparse log artifacts when reporting compiler bugs.
[09:22.96]文章建议用户报告编译器错误时附上 tlparse 日志。
[09:29.64]It also mentions TORCH_TRACE as part of this clearer reporting workflow.
[09:29.64]文章还提到用 TORCH_TRACE 帮助把问题报告得更清楚。
[09:35.34]Ava: One final change is the release cadence for 2026.
[09:35.34]Ava：最后一项变化是 2026 年的发布频率。
[09:40.39]Brian: Yes.
[09:40.39]Brian：对。
[09:40.68]The expected cadence increases from quarterly releases to one release every two months.
[09:40.68]预计将从每季度发布一次，改为每两个月发布一次。
[09:46.80]The article refers readers to the published release schedule.
[09:46.80]文章请读者查看已公布的发布日程。
[09:51.45]Ava: More frequent releases mean faster access to improvements, but also more upgrade decisions.
[09:51.45]Ava：发布更频繁，用户能更快用上改进，但也得更频繁地决定是否升级。
[09:58.40]Brian: That's a reasonable implication.
[09:58.40]Brian：这样理解很合理。
[10:00.89]The release itself simply states the new schedule and encourages users to try 2.
[10:00.89]此次发布只说明了新日程，并鼓励用户试用 2.
[10:07.11]10 and report issues.
[10:07.11]10 版并反馈问题。
[10:09.09]Ava: Let's make the practical advice concrete.
[10:09.09]Ava：说说具体该怎么做吧。
[10:11.83]If I'm a framework engineer, what should I test first?
[10:11.83]如果我是框架工程师，应该先测什么？
[10:15.78]Brian: First, check your torch. compile workflow on Python 3. 14. Python 3.
[10:15.78]Brian：首先，在 Python 3.14 上检查你的 torch.compile 工作流；Python 3.
[10:21.58]14t, the freethreaded build, is experimentally supported as well.
[10:21.58]14t 这个自由线程构建版也获得了实验性支持。
[10:27.13]Second, try Combo Kernels and varlen_attn() in isolated experiments because those APIs are unstable and have specific hardware or backend limits.
[10:27.13]其次，单独试验 Combo Kernels 和 varlen_attn()，因为这些 API 尚不稳定，而且对硬件或后端有特定限制。
[10:39.86]Ava: And for numerical issues?
[10:39.86]Ava：数值问题呢？
[10:42.28]Brian: Enable deterministic algorithms, then use DebugMode with tensor hashing to compare two model versions.
[10:42.28]Brian：开启确定性算法，再用 DebugMode 和张量哈希比较两个模型版本。
[10:49.52]Log the dispatched calls and compiled Triton kernels, and add dispatch hooks if you need custom annotations.
[10:49.52]记录实际调用和编译后的 Triton 内核；需要自定义标注时，再添加分发钩子。
[10:57.53]Ava: Before we close, give us the three-point recap.
[10:57.53]Ava：结束前，请用三点总结一下。
[11:01.48]Brian: First, performance: Combo Kernels reduce kernel launch overhead, varlen_attn() handles ragged and packed sequences, DnXgeev improves the eigenvalue decomposition path, and Intel GPU support expands.
[11:01.48]Brian：第一，性能：Combo Kernels 减少内核启动开销，varlen_attn() 处理长度不一和打包的序列，DnXgeev 改进特征值分解流程，Intel GPU 支持也得到扩展。
[11:18.14]Second, numerical confidence: torch.
[11:18.14]第二，数值可靠性：torch.compile
[11:21.17]compile respects deterministic mode, and DebugMode helps locate divergence with runtime logs and tensor hashes.
[11:21.17]遵循确定性模式；DebugMode 借助运行时日志和张量哈希定位差异。
[11:30.51]Third, ecosystem direction: TorchScript is deprecated, tlparse and TORCH_TRACE improve compiler bug reports, and 2026 moves to a two-month release cadence.
[11:30.51]第三，生态方向：TorchScript 已弃用，tlparse 和 TORCH_TRACE 改进编译器问题报告，2026 年起改为每两个月发布一次。
[11:43.90]Ava: So the message is faster execution, clearer numerical debugging, and a faster-moving project.
[11:43.90]Ava：也就是说，运行更快，数值问题更容易排查，项目更新也更频繁。
[11:51.72]Brian: Exactly.
[11:51.72]Brian：没错。
